tell me "━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━"
tell me "🔢 SECTION 3: PRIME NUMBERS & FACTORIZATION"
tell me "━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━"
tell me ""

fn is_prime_number(num) {
    if num < 2 {
        return 0
    }
    
    today i is 2
    while i * i <= num {
        if num % i == 0 {
            return 0
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
    
    return 1
}

fn check_primes_range(start, end) {
    tell me "Prime numbers between " + start + " and " + end + ":"
    today primes is []
    
    today counter is start
    while counter <= end {
        if is_prime_number(counter) == 1 {
            tell me "  ✓ " + counter
        }
        counter = counter + 1
    }
    tell me ""
}

# Test: Find primes from 1 to 20
check_primes_range(1, 20)

# Test: Check if specific numbers are prime
tell me "Prime Check:"
tell me "  Is 17 prime? " + is_prime_number(17)
tell me "  Is 16 prime? " + is_prime_number(16)
tell me ""


